The bug: the loop uses `i <= diff`, evicting `diff+1` entries (so even `diff == 0` evicts one). Fix:Fixed. In `simplelru/lru.go:161`, the eviction loop used `i <= diff`, removing `diff+1` entries — so it evicted one entry even when `size >= Len()` (diff = 0). Changed to `i < diff`. Tests pass (including a `-1` case in the existing test, which the fix also resolves since the loop now never over-evicts).